# Shared loop profile: KineX (pr-loop + scope-loop)
# REST queues only — no project board required for selection.
# Checkout: seeka/KineX → GitHub Seeka-Ltd/KineX
#
# Regenerate (optional, board-less):
#   pr-loop-setup kinex --repo-dir /Users/fstrauf/01_code/seeka/KineX --force
#
# Usage:
#   pr-loop --profile kinex --agent kimi
#   scope-loop --profile kinex --agent kimi
#
# Enqueue: gh issue edit N -R Seeka-Ltd/KineX --add-label ready

REPO=Seeka-Ltd/KineX
REPO_DIR=/Users/fstrauf/01_code/seeka/KineX

# 0 = agents do not update kanban. Selection is REST labels only.
ORCH_BOARD=0

# Default branch is `master` (not main) — the orchestrator's classic path
# falls back to origin/master correctly; just don't hardcode main anywhere.

# Leave PRs for humans. This is a shared company repo — the loop opens the
# PR, runs review + ship gate, marks ready, and stops. A human approves and
# merges. (Set ORCH_AUTO_MERGE=1 only if that policy ever changes.)
ORCH_AUTO_MERGE=0

# Ship gate: NOT here — one home per fact. The gate command lives in the
# product repo's AGENTS.md ("Testing → Automated Ship Gate"); the
# orchestrator's Phase 5 resolves it from there (branch 2). Do not copy the
# command into this profile.

# Phase 2.5 React control scan: react-doctor/shadscan are installed but this
# is Blazor Server + Tailwind, not React — both scanners fail-open/skip.
#
# NuGet: Syncfusion packages come from the private GitHub Packages feed
# (NuGet.config). dotnet restore needs the machine's existing GH credentials;
# if restore fails in the loop, that's a credentials issue, not a code issue.

# Default skill: generic (no KineX overlay — profile + AGENTS.md carry the
# repo specifics).
